---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="How Cheshire Stoneworks handles the personal data you send through this website, including the enquiry form. UK GDPR privacy notice."
  noindex
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="notice notice--review">
        REVIEW: this is a draft skeleton, not legal advice. Check it against the ICO's guidance on
        privacy notices and have it reviewed before the site goes live. Items in square brackets need
        your input.
      </p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        {site.legal.registeredName}, company number {site.legal.companyNumber}, registered office
        {site.legal.registeredOffice}. We are the data controller for the personal data described
        here. Contact: {site.contact.email}.
      </p>
      <p class="muted">[TODO: confirm whether you are registered with the ICO and add the registration number if so.]</p>

      <h2>What we collect and why</h2>
      <h3>When you send an enquiry</h3>
      <p>
        The enquiry form asks for your name, phone number, email address, postcode, details about your
        kitchen, and optionally a message and a file such as a plan, sketch or photo. We use this to
        reply to you, to check you are within our service area, to give you a price, and, if you go
        ahead, to book and carry out the work.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our lawful basis is that this processing is necessary for steps you have asked us to take
        before entering into a contract, and then for performing that contract (UK GDPR Article
        6(1)(b)). Where we keep records after a job for warranty or accounting reasons, the basis is
        our legal obligations and legitimate interests.
      </p>
      <h3>When you phone, email or message us</h3>
      <p>We keep the details you give us for the same purposes as above.</p>
      <h3>Technical data</h3>
      <p>
        Our hosting provider, Cloudflare, processes your IP address and request details in order to
        serve the site and to protect it from abuse. The enquiry form uses Cloudflare Turnstile to
        block automated spam; Turnstile processes limited browser and network information for that
        purpose. See Cloudflare's own privacy policy for details.
      </p>
      {site.cloudflareAnalyticsToken ? (
        <p>
          We use Cloudflare Web Analytics, which is cookieless and does not track you across sites or
          build a profile of you.
        </p>
      ) : (
        <p>We do not run analytics on this site.</p>
      )}

      <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
      <p>
        Enquiries are forwarded from the website to our own job management systems. [TODO: name them,
        e.g. n8n (self-hosted by us) and ServiceM8 (job management software; state where it is hosted
        and its role as a processor).] If you go ahead with a job, we share the specification and your
        delivery address with the fabricator who cuts the stone, and with our own fitters. We do not
        sell or otherwise share your data for marketing.
      </p>
      <p class="muted">[TODO: list every processor and whether any data leaves the UK, for example if ServiceM8 hosts data in Australia. State the safeguard, such as the UK IDTA or Addendum.]</p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        Enquiries that do not become a job: [TODO: period, e.g. 12 months] from the last contact, then
        deleted. Jobs we carry out: for the length of the guarantee plus [TODO: period], and financial
        records for six years after the end of the tax year as HMRC requires.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        This site sets no non-essential cookies, so there is no cookie banner. Cloudflare may set a
        strictly necessary cookie as part of its bot protection, which is exempt from consent under
        PECR. If we add anything that needs consent in future, this page and the site will change.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask us for a copy of your data, ask us to correct or delete it, object to or restrict
        how we use it, and ask for it in a portable format. Email {site.contact.email}. You can also
        complain to the Information Commissioner's Office at ico.org.uk.
      </p>

      <p class="muted">Last updated: [TODO: date].</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
